Geographic data in data.js
==========================

data.js contains simplified, re-projected geometry derived from the
following sources. It is not covered by the MIT license in LICENSE.

1. Canton outlines (window.GEO.ch.cantons)
   Derived from OpenStreetMap data via the click_that_hood project.
   © OpenStreetMap contributors — https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright
   Made available under the Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0:
   https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/
   As a derivative database, this portion of data.js is likewise
   distributed under the ODbL 1.0.

2. Ticino districts (window.GEO.ti.districts)
   Derived from swissBOUNDARIES3D via the swiss-maps package.
   Source: Federal Office of Topography swisstopo.

3. Rivers and lakes (rivers, lakes in window.GEO.ch and window.GEO.ti)
   Derived from swissTLMRegio hydrography.
   Source: Federal Office of Topography swisstopo.

   swisstopo data is open government data, free to use (including
   commercially) provided the source is credited:
   https://www.swisstopo.admin.ch/en/terms-of-use-free-geodata-and-geoservices

4. Town positions (window.GEO.ti.cities)
   Hand-placed from LV95 coordinates; no third-party rights.


Canton flags in flags/
======================

The 26 SVG flags in flags/ come from Wikimedia Commons and are public
domain. flags/SOURCES.md lists the file page, author and licence of each
one. They are not covered by the MIT license in LICENSE.

These are official insignia. Under the Swiss Coat of Arms Protection Act
(Wappenschutzgesetz, SR 232.21), anyone may use cantonal flags, provided
the use is not misleading. Cantonal coats of arms (shields) are reserved
to the cantons. This site uses the flags only to teach which flag
belongs to which canton.
